local-tts is free software under the GNU General Public License, version 3 or later (LICENSE). The Python edition
uses Piper (https://github.com/OHF-Voice/piper1-gpl, GPL-3.0) and espeak-ng (GPL-3.0), installed as dependencies.

The JavaScript edition includes espeak-ng (https://github.com/espeak-ng/espeak-ng, GPL-3.0-or-later, commit 724808c,
the one Piper 1.8 uses) compiled to WebAssembly with its bundled ucd-tools, and espeak-ng's language data as built by
piper-tts 1.8.0; espeak/build.sh rebuilds the module from source. Its phoneme handling follows Piper's espeakbridge.c,
phonemize_espeak.py and voice.py, and its word-timing model patch follows Piper's patch_voice_with_alignment.py. It uses
ONNX Runtime Web (https://github.com/microsoft/onnxruntime, MIT), installed as a dependency.

The text preparation layer, ttsprep (local_tts/textprep.py and javascript/src/textprep.ts with pyre.ts), is under the
Apache License 2.0 (LICENSE-APACHE); it can be reused under that licence on its own.

Voice models are not included. They are downloaded from their original sources and keep their own licences; each
voice's licence, training data and credit line are in local_tts/data/voices.json and shown by `local-tts voices` and
Voice.credit. Voice scores come from Loudness.ai's open study LA-RB-2026-003 (CC BY 4.0):
https://loudness.ai/research/piper-tts-voices-ranked/
